# The machine outliner asks more of a piece that stands where cold code may run: a call and a return are paid each time. A generic version runs only where a test at an entrance has failed,
# which is expected of no call, so all of its code is taken like code behind a rare edge, in a program of any size. The typed body keeps its marks.
#   f1 takesString is called in a loop. f1 stays the entrance, f3 is the typed body, f4 the generic version
# FORM: AsRead
# OPTIONS: disable=pass:InlineCalls
# RUN: generate-code units
# RUN(ROLES): pipeline SplitBehindEntryChecks
# ROLES: function f1 name="takesString" {{*}} role=EntryChecks
# ROLES: function f4 name="takesString" {{*}} role=GenericVersion
# CHECK-LABEL: f4: size=
# CHECK-NEXT: units {{*}} mayRun=0
# PROGRAM-OF: ../../pipeline/an-entrance-falls-into-its-typed-body.ir
